Z||000001||88 Fiero||09-01-99||09:56 PM||||GWMORAN....FOCOA has move to Anaheim...the new address is 1598 South Anaheim Boulevard, Anaheim, CA  92805. Tel. No. is 714-917-2007 and Fax No. is 714-917-2161. I know this because Phil's son Keith (Fiero Doc)is a very close freind of mine. You are lucky you got one of their Headers.. The guy who designs them is the same guy who makes the headers for the Buick Grand Nationals...it's been Dynoed and I think you are getting about 20 to 25% extra....
Z||000002||GWMORGAN||09-01-99||10:21 PM||||Thanx for info "88" I didn't I would be gaining that much h.p. I forgot to mention thay are jet hot coated (black) which they (FOCCA) say should help keep the heat down and make them more durable.
Z||000003||GWMORGAN||09-01-99||10:43 PM||||"88" FIERO....can you or anyone say how do re-route the sensor from the stock air filter housing also the pipe which runs from the air induction hose to the motor (firewall side)? I'm planning on installing a cold air induction system with the filter attached to one end. Do you know of a company/person who sells them?  Any info will be GREATLY appreciated.
Z||000004||88 Fiero||09-02-99||09:08 AM||||GWMORGAN....Keith will be selling this RAM Air tube soon..it will be expensive tho'...He said he will start around 25 pieces of this for the price of $200.00+...You can make one for yourself... I made one for myself..Looks good...bring your car to a local muffler place and let them know what you want to do...take off the left side grill so you have a lot of space to work on... take the factory air filter housing and it's plumbing off the car. when you do this you will notice that there is a hole in the wall...get a wire hanger and start making a pattern on how you want to route your ram air tube... be sure to check always check your cars deck lid hinges...what I mean is that when you close your deck lid it's not hitting your ram air tube... have your muffler guy give a few distance of your ram air tube from the hinges of the deck lid. Now...the tube has to come out of the hole in the wall then bent it down...that's where your K&N filter hooks up...that way your car is getting fresh air from the outside and not the inside of the engine compartment as most common ram air tube from import cars....the sensor on the other hand...what you do is cut out the nut the screws your sensors on the factory air filter box...cut a hole on your ram air tube and weld this nut and this is where your sensor gets it's new home...The other hose breather that connects the front of the valve covers is again put a hole on your ram air tube...the same position as your rubber air hose...and weld a tube in the probably about an inch long...connect a rubber hose on this and attached it to the existing air breather pipe...on mine I cut my existing air breather pipe in half and connect a long rubber hose...also I welded the nut on top of the ram air tube...that way when I wash my car and drip inside...water will not build around the sensor it will just drip all the way down...once you have this ram air you will notice how much the fiero V6 cars breath!!! Mannn!!! you can hear it....try and see if you can use a 3 inch pipe if not you can use a 2 1/2...good luck and let me know....
Z||000005||GWMORGAN||09-02-99||10:49 AM||||"88" Fiero...Thanks for the info. I will let you know the outcome.
